for uppercase

For uppercase letters (A–Z) 👇

✅ Correct hashing
vector<int> hash(26, 0);
hash[s[j] - 'A']++;

Why this works

ASCII values:

'A' = 65
'B' = 66
...
'Z' = 90


So:

'A' - 'A' = 0
'B' - 'A' = 1
...
'Z' - 'A' = 25


Perfect mapping to indices 0–25 ✔️

If string has BOTH uppercase + lowercase

Option 1️⃣: Use ASCII hash (simplest)

vector<int> hash(256, 0);
hash[s[j]]++;


Option 2️⃣: Separate arrays

vector<int> lower(26, 0), upper(26, 0);

if (s[j] >= 'a' && s[j] <= 'z')
    lower[s[j] - 'a']++;
else if (s[j] >= 'A' && s[j] <= 'Z')
    upper[s[j] - 'A']++;

Quick memory trick 🧠

'a' → lowercase

'A' → uppercase

subtract the starting letter of the range